# %msil_canon and %msil_mdcanon (plan 5.12.3; M16): canonical listing v1 of
# an assembly (plan 5.7.10), the layout-independent text that later
# milestones compare between assemblers, dumpers and linkers. Until M17
# %msil_canon is mdcanon (msil/utils/mdtools/mdcanon.cs, plan 5.7.11) on the
# host's dotnet; from M17 it is llvm-cil-dump --canonical, which must print
# the same bytes. Inputs/canon-listing.il has one of each construct that the
# 5.12.6 normalizations act on and more (its header comment lists them); it
# is assembled with %ilasm -dll and listed three times:
# (DEF)  the default options: header lines in 5.7.10's order, members sorted
#        by name and signature, operands and clauses as 5.7.10 spells them;
# (DECL) --order=decl --forms=canon: members in table order, short branches
#        and ldc.i4.s in their long forms;
# (NORM) the five plan 5.12.6 normalizations that an ilasm image exercises:
#        hash=* (--assembly-hash=ignore), no .param line for a Param row with
#        Flags 0 (--params=drop; the [opt] one stays), no ' initlocals'
#        without .locals (--initlocals=ignore-without-locals), '*' for the
#        P/Invoke module and no moduleref line (--pinvoke-module=strip), and
#        the P/Invoke method's access bits cleared (--pinvoke-access=ignore).
#        --snan=quiet needs an image with a float32 signaling NaN, which ilasm
#        never writes (M17.f patches one).
# The second input, coverage.il at the end of this file (split-file), has the
# rest of what the listing prints; its header comment lists it. %python
# prepends the UTF-8 BOM that ilasm needs to read the names a～ and a😀 as
# UTF-8, and it is assembled with %ilasm -exe and listed so:
# (COV)   the default options: the entrypoint header line, a namespaced class
#         with a nested class, an interface, a literal field and a property,
#         an explicit layout, escaped names, UTF-8 (not UTF-16) name order,
#         general arrays as plan section 12's row '5.7.10 amended (`<type>` in
#         signatures, general arrays)' spells them, float and negative integer
#         operands, a MethodSpec, TypeSpec and nested TypeRef tokens, an
#         escaped ldstr, and a filter and a finally clause;
# (STRIP) --scopes=strip: '[*]' for AssemblyRef scopes, in signatures too,
#         no '[mscorlib]' left and no assemblyref line (one line fewer);
# (STATS) --stats-only: a line per present table in id order, the four heaps
#         and the image; the numbers are regexes, because they depend on the
#         ilasm (Framework or NuGet). --stats appends exactly these lines to
#         the default listing.
# The expected lines were written from 5.7.10, 5.12.6 and that row; the
# Framework and the NuGet ilasm's images both give them. FileCheck runs with
# --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace, so a pattern starts right after
# the colon and pins the indentation, and each listing's line count pins its
# end. Last, %msil_mdcanon --out-dir (one process for many files) must write
# the same bytes as the default listings on stdout.
# REQUIRES: msil-mdcanon

# RUN: rm -rf %t.d && split-file %s %t.d
# RUN: %ilasm -dll -output=%t.d/canon.dll %S/Inputs/canon-listing.il
# RUN: %msil_canon %t.d/canon.dll > %t.d/default.canon
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.d/default.canon %s --check-prefix=DEF --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
# RUN: count 44 < %t.d/default.canon
# RUN: %msil_canon --order=decl --forms=canon %t.d/canon.dll > %t.d/decl.canon
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.d/decl.canon %s --check-prefix=DECL --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
# RUN: count 44 < %t.d/decl.canon
# RUN: %msil_canon --assembly-hash=ignore --params=drop --initlocals=ignore-without-locals --pinvoke-module=strip --pinvoke-access=ignore %t.d/canon.dll > %t.d/norm.canon
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.d/norm.canon %s --check-prefix=NORM --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
# RUN: count 41 < %t.d/norm.canon
# RUN: %python -c "import sys; d = open(sys.argv[1], 'rb').read(); open(sys.argv[2], 'wb').write(b'\xef\xbb\xbf' + d)" %t.d/coverage.il %t.d/coverage-bom.il
# RUN: %ilasm -exe -output=%t.d/coverage.exe %t.d/coverage-bom.il
# RUN: %msil_canon %t.d/coverage.exe > %t.d/coverage.canon
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.d/coverage.canon %s --check-prefix=COV --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
# RUN: count 79 < %t.d/coverage.canon
# RUN: %msil_canon --scopes=strip %t.d/coverage.exe > %t.d/strip.canon
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.d/strip.canon %s --check-prefix=STRIP --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace --implicit-check-not=assemblyref '--implicit-check-not=[mscorlib]'
# RUN: count 78 < %t.d/strip.canon
# RUN: %msil_canon --stats-only %t.d/coverage.exe > %t.d/stats.canon
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.d/stats.canon %s --check-prefix=STATS --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
# RUN: count 24 < %t.d/stats.canon
# RUN: %msil_canon --stats %t.d/coverage.exe > %t.d/stats-append.canon
# RUN: cat %t.d/coverage.canon %t.d/stats.canon > %t.d/stats-expected.canon
# RUN: diff %t.d/stats-expected.canon %t.d/stats-append.canon
# RUN: %msil_mdcanon --out-dir %t.d/out %t.d/canon.dll %t.d/coverage.exe
# RUN: diff %t.d/default.canon %t.d/out/canon.dll.canon
# RUN: diff %t.d/coverage.canon %t.d/out/coverage.exe.canon

